WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.770
Around 2.1 billion people cook on
open fires or inefficient stoves.

2
00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:09.070
A solar oven needs no
fuel to buy or collect,

3
00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.870
and makes no smoke.

4
00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:14.750
In rural Senegal,
researchers ran a fair test.

5
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.110
465 households got an oven first.

6
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:21.210
325 waited six months.

7
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:22.450
Free sunshine.

8
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:23.730
No smoke.

9
00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:26.610
Yet most women still cooked on wood.

10
00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.010
Did the ovens break?

11
00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.670
Was the sun too weak?

12
00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:31.890
Or was it something else?

13
00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:35.630
In this mission, you'll learn what
makes a technology appropriate,

14
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.650
and test a water roller against that idea.

15
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.190
Then you'll read the
Senegal trial's results,

16
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:42.790
like a researcher.

17
00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:47.490
Your mission: find out why free
sunshine did not replace the wood fire.
